A||||3||Mark||Steering Rack Play||||1||
Z||000000||Mark||09-25-2000||06:42 PM||||When I force the front wheels (at the 3 and 9 o'clock positions) against the steering wheel lock, I notice slight up and down play in the inner tie rods on both driver and passenger sides of my steering rack. This is a real bummer since my car only has 39K miles and there appears to be no slop whatsoever in the rack and pinion gears. Is this another case of the infamous worn rack bushing or maybe worn tie rods?  Is there any spec for allowable motion? How can I tell for sure if it is rack bushings or tie rods? <BR> <BR>Also, I only see the passenger side bushing listed on Rodney's site. Is the driver side bushing not available or impossible to replace?  In a search on this subject, I seem to recall someone claiming that they still had up and down play even after replaced everything (rack, inner tie rods, and tie rod ends). I also read that replacing the passenger side bushing somehow cures the driver side.  Is this for real?  Thanks in advance.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-25-2000||10:06 PM||||I had always thought there was some play in the front suspension, ball joints and tie rods when all was right with the world. Without being there, seeing if there is any unusual tire wear etc, it's sort of hard to say if the movement you are seeing is critical. If you need a bushing repair, Rodney's kit will do the job. Pssenger side bushings usually fail first. As long as your car isn't an 88, you can get replacement steering racks reasonably and ball joints and other stuff reasonably.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||09-26-2000||05:39 PM||||Lar, it's an '86.  No unusual tire wear.  It just doesn't have the strong on-center feel that I like.  The car seems to want to drift one way and then the other.  This could be front tires, although they are in great shape and are stock size (205/60-15).<P>I'm still confused on the rack bushings.  Why is only the passenger side available, or am I just missing something?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||09-26-2000||05:42 PM||||It could also be wheel alignment.  I plan to get an alignment when I replace rear struts.  But I need to make sure the suspension and steering are all OK before I do that.||||reg||1
